 margin, little waste. Good.\n- **3** (every day, about 1.15× on product 0, 1.1× on product 1): close to the right margin. Good.\n- **0** (every other day, about 1.1× on both): cheaper fixed costs and a reasonable margin. Good.\n- **6** (every other day, 1.0×): some shortages, but the two-day batches smooth out daily swings and it saves about 315. Borderline, but better than the ones below.\n- **2** (every day, exactly the forecast): it runs short all the time because real demand averages about 1.046× forecast, and it pays the full daily ordering cost.\n- **4** (1.3× on product 0, 1.0× on product 1): it wastes product 0 and runs short of product 1, so it loses both ways.\n- **7** (1.3× and 1.2×): excess keeps piling up. I estimate roughly 50 a day in written-off product 0, about 28 a day in product 1, plus holding.\n- **5** (every 3 days): holding a 3-day batch of product 1 costs more than the fixed costs it saves. Around day 17, about 200 units arrive at once (143 of product 1, 57 of product 0) on top of what's already in stock, so some may be lost to the 208-unit capacity limit.\n\nMy least confident call is putting candidate 6 ahead of 2 and 7."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5054, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5054}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:14:49.233Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWCChU86VjB28vgSdcFU"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01YP7C2rL4pRLKvux1296f2s", "name